  "story": {
    "premise": "Publication of the correction triggers a surge of hearing queries against an unstable archive service. Two consecutive failures must open the circuit. Silence during cooldown is deliberate; after exactly two ticks, only one request may probe the archive until a real success or failure resolves it.",
    "submission": "Submit a three-cell closed/open/half-open controller. Preserve admitted request payloads, reset closed-state failure streaks on success, and never admit a second half-open request.",
    "diagnostics": "The exhaustive oracle covers 3,478 bounded command streams and separates rolling failure streaks, cooldown boundaries, half-open singleton probes, probe failure, and recovery.",
    "hints": [
      "Opening time matters only while open.",
      "A probe is a state transition, not an ordinary admission.",
      "Success before a probe resets a closed failure streak but cannot close an already open circuit."
    ]
  }
